        <mxCell id="root" value="MOSA" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="142.0" width="74.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="data" value="Data" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="170.0" y="74.0" width="111.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="views" value="Omics Data" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="337.0" y="40.0" width="90.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="cond" value="Conditionals Metadata" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="337.0" y="108.0" width="104.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="model" value="Model" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="170.0" y="210.0" width="74.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="vae" value="MOSA VAE" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="337.0" y="176.0" width="76.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="mofa" value="MOFA" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECECEC;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#222222;fontSize=13;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="337.0" y="244.0" width="74.0" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1001" style="startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;endArrow=oval;endFill=1;endSize=9;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="data"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="114.0" y="165.0" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="170.0" y="97.0" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1002" style="startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;endArrow=oval;endFill=1;endSize=9;" edge="1" parent="1" source="root" target="model"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="114.0" y="165.0" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="170.0" y="233.0" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1003" style="startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;endArrow=oval;endFill=1;endSize=9;" edge="1" parent="1" source="data" target="views"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="281.0" y="97.0" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="337.0" y="63.0" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1004" style="startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;endArrow=oval;endFill=0;endSize=9;" edge="1" parent="1" source="data" target="cond"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="281.0" y="97.0" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="337.0" y="131.0" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1005" style="startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;endArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="model" target="vae"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="244.0" y="233.0" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="337.0" y="199.0" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1006" style="startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;endArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="model" target="mofa"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="244.0" y="233.0" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="337.0" y="267.0" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1007" style="curved=1;endArrow=none;startArrow=none;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;rounded=0;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="270.3" y="223.4" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="270.3" y="242.6" as="targetPoint"/><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="276.0" y="233.0"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="k1015" value="Notes" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=14;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="388.0" width="520" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1016" value="•  A MOSA run composes the model-agnostic Data sub-tree (fm_data) with exactly one Model — an alternative (XOR) group: MOSA VAE or MOFA." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="410.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1017" value="•  No cross-tree constraints apply at this level: model choice is unconstrained by data. Configuration constraints live in the sub-trees (fm_data, fm_vae)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="430.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1018" value="•  Both models implement the MultiOmicModel ABC (fit / transform / reconstruct / save / load), so the shared Data definition benchmarks them on identical inputs." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="450.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1019" value="•  Omics Data (≥ 1 modality) is the reconstruction target: continuous views are standard-scaled, discrete views left unscaled, missing entries masked and zero-imputed." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="470.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1020" value="     Each modality is encoded and decoded by its own view-specific network (multi-view)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="490.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1021" value="•  Conditionals Metadata = per-sample side information aligned to every modality; its effect is feature- and model-specific:" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="510.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1022" value="     –  Model Type (effectively mandatory — both models key on it): one-hot batch label. VAE: conditional input, adversarial-discriminator target, class-balanced sampling.  MOFA: multi-group key." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="530.0" width="900" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1023" value="     –  Tissue (optional, use_tissue): appended to the conditioning vector and used as the contrastive-loss target — MOSA VAE only." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="550.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1024" value="     –  Mutations (optional, use_mutations): appended to the conditioning vector — MOSA VAE only." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="570.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="k1025" value="•  MOSA VAE = conditional multi-view VAE (fm_vae); MOFA = linear factor-analysis baseline (mofapy2 / mofax) that ignores Tissue and Mutations." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="590.0" width="820" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
